-- title:
--   Existence and uniqueness of the reduced place on a chart
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $F$ be a field extension of $L$ and $\bar F$ a field extension of $k$, both one-variable function fields in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors of degree $0$ exist for every nonzero element, every place has residue field finite over the base field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank $1$). Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with reduction $\bar F$: a valuation subring $\mathcal O = R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,F\,c \in \mathcal O \iff c \in A$, together with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res} \colon \mathcal O \to \bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, which sends the image of $a \in A$ to the image in $\bar F$ of the residue of $a$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has a scalar multiple $c \cdot f \in \mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{res}(c\cdot f) \neq 0$. Let $x \in \mathcal O$ be such that $\bar x = \mathrm{res}\,x$ is transcendental over $k$, the degree $[\bar F : k(\bar x)]$ is positive, and $[F : L(x)] = [\bar F : k(\bar x)]$ (finite ranks over the intermediate fields generated by $x$, resp. $\bar x$); assume moreover the chart hypothesis that every $h \in \bar F$ integral over the subalgebra $k[\bar x]$ is of the form $\mathrm{res}\,f$ for some $f \in \mathcal O$ integral over $L[x]$. Finally let $P$ be a place of $F$ over $L$, that is, a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $L$, different from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, and suppose there is $a \in A$ with $x - \mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,F\,a$ in the nonunits (maximal ideal) of $P$. Then there exists a unique place $Q$ of $\bar F$ over $k$ with the property that for every $h \in \mathcal O$ integral over $L[x]$ and every $a \in A$ with $h - \mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,F\,a$ in the nonunits of $P$, the difference $\mathrm{res}\,h - \mathrm{algebraMap}\,k\,\bar F(\mathrm{residue}\,a)$ lies in the nonunits of $Q$.
--
--   This is the pointwise form of Deuring's reduction of places in the situation of good reduction, carried out on the affine chart determined by $x$: a place of $F/L$ at which $x$ is finite with value in $A$ specialises to a unique place of $\bar F/k$. It is the basis for the comparison of orders and divisors under reduction, being cited by the statements that build the induced map on places and that compare $\mathrm{ord}$ along the reduction for elements integral over $L[x]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation_existsUnique_place_forall_residue_sub_mem_nonunits.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
